 "title": "Шанс для новичка  (A Chance for the Newcomer)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "max": "Макс"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max has been given a first job: peeling stickers off bananas. He tries to pitch his chicken in cream sauce to the chef, who laughs at him, and then, unexpectedly, gives him a test: a dessert for an important guest. Here it is in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, у меня есть отличная идея.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я могу приготовить своё фирменное блюдо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Это нежная курица в сливочном соусе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Великолепная идея от неизвестного человека.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты пришёл на мою кухню случайно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Лучше чисти бананы дальше!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Зачем вообще снимать эти наклейки?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Для идеального порядка во вселенной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Но я умею готовить прекрасные десерты.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Хорошо, я дам тебе один шанс.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "К нам пришёл наш постоянный гость.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты приготовишь десерт для Элеоноры Андреевны.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Если десерт понравится, ты останешься здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Договорились, шеф! Я сделаю лучший десерт.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go back over the pitch.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, у меня есть отличная идея.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, I have an excellent idea.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "У меня есть",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"at me there is\", the full form of \"I have\". Earlier it was without it, with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "есть",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " left out.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я могу приготовить своё фирменное блюдо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I can prepare my signature dish.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Могу",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"I can\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Фирменное",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " comes from the word for company, so a ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "фирменное блюдо",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the house's own dish.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Это нежная курица в сливочном соусе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It is tender chicken in cream sauce.' Because ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "курица",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", chicken, is feminine, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "нежная",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", tender, ends in -aya. The word for creamy comes from the word for cream, and after ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "в",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " the sauce becomes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "соусе",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", \"in the sauce\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Великолепная идея от неизвестного человека.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A magnificent idea from an unknown person.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Великолепная",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " has the word for great inside it. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Неизвестного",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is formed with the negative prefix, so \"unknown\". Praise this big from Barinov is a joke at Max's expense.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты пришёл на мою кухню случайно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You came to my kitchen by accident.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Случайно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " comes from ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "случай",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", chance, which is also in the phrase for \"what happened\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "На мою кухню",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"to my kitchen\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Лучше чисти бананы дальше!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Better keep peeling bananas!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Лучше",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"better\", used as \"you'd better\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Чисти",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the command \"peel\", from the word for clean. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Дальше",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"further\", meaning \"keep going\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Зачем вообще снимать эти наклейки?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why peel off these stickers at all?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Зачем",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " asks \"what for?\", about purpose, where the other word for why asks about the cause. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Снимать",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"to take off\", the everyday partner of the verb from the stove, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "наклейки",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", stickers, come from the verb to glue.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Для идеального порядка во вселенной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'For ideal order in the universe.' The word for order here is the same word from \"keep order on your table\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Во вселенной",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"in the universe\": ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "в",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " becomes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "во",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " before a heavy cluster like \"vs\", just to make it sayable.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Но я умею готовить прекрасные десерты.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'But I know how to prepare wonderful desserts.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Но",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the plain \"but\", different from ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "а",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Прекрасные десерты",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is plural, so the describing word ends in \"-ye\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Хорошо, я дам тебе один шанс.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'All right, I will give you one chance.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Дам",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"I will give\", irregular and short. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Тебе",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"to you\", the friendly form.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "К нам пришёл наш постоянный гость.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Our regular guest has arrived.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Постоянный",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"regular\", and its partner means \"constantly\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "К нам пришёл",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"has come to us\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты приготовишь десерт для Элеоноры Андреевны.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You will prepare dessert for Eleonora Andreyevna.' Names change after ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "для",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", even the father's name: the first name becomes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Элеоноры",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", and the second name becomes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Андреевны",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Если десерт понравится, ты останешься здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If the dessert is liked, you will stay here.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Понравится",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"will please\", the future of the verb to please. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Останешься",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"you will stay\", the \"self\" ending included.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Договорились, шеф! Я сделаю лучший десерт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Agreed, chef! I will make the best dessert.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Договорились",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "! is the everyday \"deal!\", the finished partner of the verb from the morning after. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Лучший",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " already means \"best\", with no need for \"very\". Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, у меня есть отличная идея.",
   "gap": 0.5
